WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.274
- Well my motto, I was always
taught when I was young,

00:00:02.274 --> 00:00:03.888
is nothing's going to get
handed to you on a plate.

00:00:03.888 --> 00:00:05.340
So you have literally got to go out

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:07.007
and fight for everything you can get.

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:07.847
But it's out there.

00:00:07.847 --> 00:00:11.051
(light music)

00:00:11.051 --> 00:00:12.132
Me and my grand dad were trying to fix

00:00:12.132 --> 00:00:14.284
a curtain rail to a plasterboard wall.

00:00:14.284 --> 00:00:15.855
And it kept coming down, time after time.

00:00:15.855 --> 00:00:19.030
So we went out to the local hardware store

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:21.471
and bought all the fixings
you could think of.

00:00:21.471 --> 00:00:22.482
Nothing would work, so we literally,

00:00:22.482 --> 00:00:24.473
he had a small, little garden shed,

00:00:24.473 --> 00:00:27.304
so we went out in there
and mocked up something,

00:00:27.304 --> 00:00:28.727
nothing like what it looks like today.

00:00:28.727 --> 00:00:30.601
But it was basically the same
action, with a wing action

00:00:30.601 --> 00:00:33.651
that spreads the load
behind the plasterboard.

00:00:33.651 --> 00:00:36.012
And then we came back in,
tried it, and it worked.

00:00:36.012 --> 00:00:38.568
And that was kind of
the, the moment, really.

00:00:38.568 --> 00:00:40.764
But it was just to solve a problem.

00:00:40.764 --> 00:00:45.167
When I was back at school,
when swine flu happened.

00:00:45.167 --> 00:00:46.378
Everyone was going mad
about having to have

00:00:46.378 --> 00:00:47.724
their hands clean and everything.

00:00:47.724 --> 00:00:49.601
So I went into the local Asda,

00:00:49.601 --> 00:00:51.228
and I think they were on sale for a pound,

00:00:51.228 --> 00:00:53.057
so I bought everything they had in stock,

00:00:53.057 --> 00:00:54.472
and then went to school and was selling it

00:00:54.472 --> 00:00:56.466
for two, three pound, making a profit.

00:00:56.466 --> 00:00:57.827
And I ended up getting
told off by the teachers,

00:00:57.827 --> 00:00:59.452
so I stopped that.

00:00:59.452 --> 00:01:02.217
And then I ended up
leaving school at just 13.

00:01:02.217 --> 00:01:04.816
And I ended up starting
my own tutoring agency.

00:01:04.816 --> 00:01:07.823
So it's kind of a personal
agency that found tutors

00:01:07.823 --> 00:01:11.990
for people and put them
in touch with the clients.

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:16.090
I mean the time with GripIt,
we've grown so rapidly,

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:17.959
going on Dragon's Den was massive for us.

00:01:17.959 --> 00:01:19.083
It gave us the money that we needed

00:01:19.083 --> 00:01:22.879
to increase production,
and then we invented

00:01:22.879 --> 00:01:24.057
a few more products since then.

00:01:24.057 --> 00:01:26.255
A few new changes to the product,

00:01:26.255 --> 00:01:28.635
and we've gone from 500
stores to 5,000 now.

00:01:28.635 --> 00:01:30.491
So it's only a short
space, like two years,

00:01:30.491 --> 00:01:31.658
so it's crazy.

00:01:33.277 --> 00:01:35.437
Biggest challenge for me
is finding the right staff,

00:01:35.437 --> 00:01:39.222
cause obviously, your business
is your baby sort of thing.

00:01:39.222 --> 00:01:40.870
So now, trying to find the right staff

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:43.072
to put in the right place in the company

00:01:43.072 --> 00:01:44.275
is my difficult challenge, trying to

00:01:44.275 --> 00:01:47.040
hand that trust over sort of thing.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.356
So what's next for GripIt is,
we're helping other inventors

00:01:49.356 --> 00:01:50.562
that have done the same to us,

00:01:50.562 --> 00:01:52.027
bringing their products to market,

00:01:52.027 --> 00:01:53.612
so we're doing that through GripIt.

00:01:53.612 --> 00:01:55.809
We're bringing out some
new products ourselves.

00:01:55.809 --> 00:01:58.405
We've just gone over to
the U.S. and Australia,

00:01:58.405 --> 00:01:59.971
gonna be a busy couple of years.

00:01:59.971 --> 00:02:03.138
(inspirational music)

